1
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,200
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,150
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,240
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:39,743 --> 00:00:42,984
Don't go, Yi Jae. Please...

5
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:54,149
Soo Bin.

6
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,034
I love you...

7
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:02,588
but you're not my dream.

8
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,172
[Final Episode]

9
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:28,588
Even if you leave, I won't let go of us.

10
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:29,924
You know what I mean.

11
00:01:29,924 --> 00:01:32,363
You don't get it.

12
00:01:32,363 --> 00:01:36,017
If I leave, that means letting us go.

13
00:01:36,017 --> 00:01:38,907
It's only two years.

14
00:01:38,907 --> 00:01:40,177
Why do we have to break up?

15
00:01:40,177 --> 00:01:44,104
If I go with you beside me,
I'll lean on you there too.

16
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,661
Then nothing will change.

17
00:01:45,661 --> 00:01:49,638
Look. You just took the chairs from me.

18
00:01:49,638 --> 00:01:51,318
- So what?
- Woo Soo Bin.

19
00:01:51,318 --> 00:01:53,115
Do you really not get it?

20
00:01:53,115 --> 00:01:55,741
If I stay with you, you'll only look at me too.

21
00:01:55,741 --> 00:01:58,909
Will you spend your life worrying about me?

22
00:02:01,095 --> 00:02:04,485
This isn't what I pictured for us.

23
00:02:04,485 --> 00:02:06,356
Not for me.

24
00:02:06,356 --> 00:02:07,377
Not for you either.

25
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:10,824
Why do you keep saying we can't stay like this?

26
00:02:13,617 --> 00:02:15,545
You said you love me.

27
00:02:18,371 --> 00:02:22,770
- You said you cared.
- That's why I'm not going to love you anymore!

28
00:02:30,266 --> 00:02:33,278
Why are you making me say something like this?

29
00:02:35,239 --> 00:02:38,113
I'm sorry. I should go.

30
00:02:59,848 --> 00:03:01,989
[2026 Bunam International
Cinema Residency Application]

31
00:03:02,662 --> 00:03:04,242
[Field: Film]

32
00:03:11,063 --> 00:03:13,478
[Applicant Name: Ju Yi Jae]

33
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:30,278
<i>Are you leaving me out because of my leg?</i>

34
00:03:30,278 --> 00:03:33,208
<i>How does some no-name college grad
just waltz in?</i>

35
00:03:33,208 --> 00:03:35,973
<i>- Calm down.
- What the...</i>

36
00:03:36,798 --> 00:03:39,344
<i>No. Nobody said anything.</i>

37
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:41,134
<i>Isn't that weird?</i>

38
00:03:41,134 --> 00:03:44,836
<i>No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.</i>

39
00:03:44,836 --> 00:03:46,840
<i>Help me, Soo Bin.</i>

40
00:03:47,896 --> 00:03:50,338
<i>Help me keep running.</i>

41
00:04:11,990 --> 00:04:13,433
Hello, sir.

42
00:04:13,433 --> 00:04:16,581
The guitar piece for our reunion scene.

43
00:04:16,581 --> 00:04:19,011
I cleaned up the noise as much as I could,

44
00:04:19,011 --> 00:04:21,306
but I couldn't remove all the set noise.

45
00:04:21,306 --> 00:04:23,566
Come on. That's my job.

46
00:04:23,566 --> 00:04:26,182
Just send me the footage, Director Ju.

47
00:04:26,182 --> 00:04:28,226
<i>Then I'll send it right now.</i>

48
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,568
But while I was organizing it, I had a thought.

49
00:04:30,568 --> 00:04:33,792
If we can't get it clean anyway,

50
00:04:33,792 --> 00:04:35,651
what if we make it sound like a gramophone?

51
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:36,985
<i>A gramophone?</i>

52
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:37,986
Yeah.

53
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:41,941
<i>That would cover the audio quality issue,</i>

54
00:04:41,941 --> 00:04:43,531
<i>and it would add to the period feel.</i>

55
00:04:43,531 --> 00:04:46,537
Please talk it over
with Director Woo and let me know.

56
00:04:46,537 --> 00:04:48,547
Okay... Oh, right.

57
00:04:48,547 --> 00:04:51,730
Is something going on with Director Woo lately?

58
00:04:52,724 --> 00:04:55,003
I don't know. Why?

59
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,377
<i>He just seems...</i>

60
00:04:58,213 --> 00:04:59,409
<i>Never mind.</i>

61
00:04:59,409 --> 00:05:02,177
<i>I'll call you later. Have a good one.</i>

62
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:03,777
Yeah.

63
00:05:26,695 --> 00:05:28,371
Alright.

64
00:05:28,371 --> 00:05:31,819
<i>♪ Shall we... ♪</i>

65
00:05:31,819 --> 00:05:32,862
Wait...

66
00:05:32,862 --> 00:05:35,043
Oh my gosh!

67
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,470
Hey!

68
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:39,115
You scared me!

69
00:05:39,115 --> 00:05:41,340
I thought about it...

70
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,592
What?

71
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,100
Are you sleep-talking?

72
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:46,180
Why are you sleeping here?

73
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:47,856
Go home already.

74
00:05:47,856 --> 00:05:51,518
Listen. That guitar piece we were going to use.

75
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:54,140
If we can't isolate it cleanly,

76
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:58,203
why not make it sound like a gramophone?

77
00:05:58,203 --> 00:06:00,781
Like it's from the street.

78
00:06:02,036 --> 00:06:05,133
Did you just talk to Director Ju?

79
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:06,350
What?

80
00:06:06,350 --> 00:06:09,643
You said the exact same thing she did.

81
00:06:09,643 --> 00:06:13,528
I came here to work on that.

82
00:06:14,996 --> 00:06:16,999
By the way...

83
00:06:16,999 --> 00:06:20,588
Who's Sim Shin?

84
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:24,718
Where did you find the hidden master?

85
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:27,178
Back up a little.

86
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:32,142
He's actor Sim Yu Geon's father.

87
00:06:32,142 --> 00:06:34,079
Awesome! Seriously?

88
00:06:34,079 --> 00:06:36,773
His playing was something else.

89
00:06:36,773 --> 00:06:41,480
No flashy technique, but it hits you hard.

90
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,611
This is exciting.

91
00:06:42,611 --> 00:06:44,510
Hold on...

92
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:46,281
Alright.

93
00:06:50,592 --> 00:06:52,236
Time to work. Please leave.

94
00:06:52,236 --> 00:06:53,247
Yeah.

95
00:06:53,247 --> 00:06:56,289
Go ahead. Do your exciting work.

96
00:06:56,289 --> 00:06:58,846
If you're staying here, pay some rent.

97
00:06:58,846 --> 00:07:02,125
If I don't push you, you always miss deadlines.

98
00:07:02,125 --> 00:07:04,363
- Just turn on the computer.
- Wait.

99
00:07:04,363 --> 00:07:08,223
How about this when Moo Gyeom gets chased?

100
00:07:12,025 --> 00:07:13,975
Are we in Africa?

101
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:16,811
This is Gyeongseong.

102
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:20,116
You really know nothing about music.

103
00:07:23,721 --> 00:07:25,447
[Final Results for
the Bunam International Cinema Residency]

104
00:07:25,447 --> 00:07:27,231
[You have been selected for
the Bunam International Cinema Residency]

105
00:07:27,231 --> 00:07:29,240
[Congratulations, Director Ju Yi Jae]

106
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:50,220
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

107
00:07:56,038 --> 00:07:57,878
Woo Soo Bin.

108
00:08:28,319 --> 00:08:30,111
Can I come in?

109
00:08:30,945 --> 00:08:33,028
Sure, come in.

110
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:39,449
Sorry. That wasn't mine to say.

111
00:08:39,449 --> 00:08:42,310
You got in, didn't you?

112
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:44,691
You came to tell me, right?

113
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:46,091
Yeah.

114
00:08:48,545 --> 00:08:50,123
Yi Jae.

115
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:53,340
Why do you look like that?

116
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,052
I'm sorry.

117
00:09:01,799 --> 00:09:03,354
Look at me.

118
00:09:05,772 --> 00:09:07,917
I was wrong.

119
00:09:09,898 --> 00:09:13,556
I came this far because I loved you.

120
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:17,653
But then I used that love to ask you to stay.

121
00:09:17,653 --> 00:09:19,744
I was so ashamed.

122
00:09:20,619 --> 00:09:25,388
I forgot my promise to give your dream back.

123
00:09:26,159 --> 00:09:28,283
I'm sorry.

124
00:09:28,283 --> 00:09:31,840
You already did.

125
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,700
Thanks to you, I found my dream again.

126
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:39,347
For the next two years,
I'll make it bigger and better.

127
00:09:46,152 --> 00:09:48,635
I know you will.

128
00:09:49,618 --> 00:09:52,539
You already shine this bright.

129
00:10:05,439 --> 00:10:07,933
Goodbye, Director Ju Yi Jae.

130
00:10:08,593 --> 00:10:12,526
Wherever you are, whatever you do,
I'll always root for you.

131
00:10:13,792 --> 00:10:15,497
Thank you.

132
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:19,901
Take care.

133
00:11:00,033 --> 00:11:02,097
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

134
00:11:02,097 --> 00:11:04,617
<i>Finally done!</i>

135
00:11:10,409 --> 00:11:11,539
<i>Cut!</i>

136
00:11:11,539 --> 00:11:13,362
<i>- Okay!
- Okay!</i>

137
00:11:35,751 --> 00:11:37,459
Ju Yi Jae!

138
00:11:51,652 --> 00:11:55,479
Take this with you.

139
00:11:56,546 --> 00:11:59,367
I hope this doesn't keep you from moving on,

140
00:11:59,367 --> 00:12:01,674
but gives you...

141
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:04,912
the strength to endure.

142
00:12:05,528 --> 00:12:08,502
Like "Gyeongseong Love Song" did for me.

143
00:12:53,863 --> 00:12:55,886
Did you tell your dad?

144
00:12:55,886 --> 00:12:58,593
That his playing will be in our film?

145
00:12:58,593 --> 00:12:59,690
Yes.

146
00:12:59,690 --> 00:13:02,493
He was thrilled.

147
00:13:02,493 --> 00:13:06,117
He watches your video
in his hospital room every day.

148
00:13:06,117 --> 00:13:08,363
I'm glad he likes it.

149
00:13:15,117 --> 00:13:16,628
Yi Jae.

150
00:13:16,628 --> 00:13:19,458
You know I'm your biggest fan, right?

151
00:13:19,458 --> 00:13:21,052
Of course I do.

152
00:13:21,052 --> 00:13:24,476
If I hadn't had you in Seoul,
where I knew no one,

153
00:13:24,476 --> 00:13:27,818
I couldn't have held on.

154
00:13:27,818 --> 00:13:32,275
The chicken you brought,
saying you couldn't finish it alone.

155
00:13:32,275 --> 00:13:36,429
The calls for no real reason.

156
00:13:36,429 --> 00:13:39,095
I knew it was all you cheering me on.

157
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,111
So...

158
00:13:45,111 --> 00:13:49,493
If it gets lonely or hard there,
you have to tell me.

159
00:13:49,493 --> 00:13:50,583
Hey.

160
00:13:50,583 --> 00:13:51,623
I'm Ju Yi Jae.

161
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:53,993
That's why I'm saying it.

162
00:13:53,993 --> 00:13:58,883
Don't suffer alone
just because you hate looking weak.

163
00:14:00,727 --> 00:14:03,374
So cheesy.

164
00:14:03,374 --> 00:14:05,400
Just have your soup.

165
00:14:14,471 --> 00:14:16,595
- Hey, Ju Young Jae!
- What?

166
00:14:16,595 --> 00:14:20,705
Just quit already!

167
00:14:20,705 --> 00:14:23,315
What is it now?

168
00:14:23,315 --> 00:14:25,642
Did you even taste it before serving it?

169
00:14:25,642 --> 00:14:27,046
Try this!

170
00:14:27,046 --> 00:14:30,353
Look at the great food critic.

171
00:14:36,526 --> 00:14:38,432
Darn it! Water!

172
00:14:38,432 --> 00:14:40,807
Water! Water!

173
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:46,358
I'll add more water.

174
00:14:46,358 --> 00:14:48,413
Sorry.

175
00:14:50,325 --> 00:14:52,061
I'll apologize for him.

176
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:57,093
You said you'd be there two years.
Why pack only winter clothes?

177
00:14:57,093 --> 00:15:01,351
I looked it up.
Mon-tree-all has all four seasons too.

178
00:15:01,351 --> 00:15:03,716
It's Montreal, idiot.

179
00:15:03,716 --> 00:15:06,282
Let her be. She can buy things there.

180
00:15:06,282 --> 00:15:09,115
Since when do you tell anyone to buy things?

181
00:15:09,115 --> 00:15:12,186
Mom. I can't take all this anyway.

182
00:15:12,186 --> 00:15:13,492
Why not?

183
00:15:13,492 --> 00:15:15,928
You're not carrying it. The plane is.

184
00:15:15,928 --> 00:15:19,787
I heard there are lots of
Korean restaurants there.

185
00:15:24,962 --> 00:15:27,252
Then take this.

186
00:15:27,252 --> 00:15:28,839
What is it?

187
00:15:28,839 --> 00:15:31,683
- Money?
- Give it back. That's for your sister.

188
00:15:31,683 --> 00:15:34,776
This has to be at least a million won!

189
00:15:36,766 --> 00:15:38,090
Come on.

190
00:15:38,090 --> 00:15:39,943
What money do you have?

191
00:15:39,943 --> 00:15:42,324
Just pay off your loan interest.

192
00:15:42,324 --> 00:15:44,020
Keep it as emergency cash.

193
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:46,400
Don't scrape by over there.

194
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,257
I said I'm fine.

195
00:15:48,257 --> 00:15:51,425
It's not like I'm leaving forever.
I'll be back soon.

196
00:15:51,425 --> 00:15:54,328
She's right. Two years will fly by.

197
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:56,654
Just think of it as sending her to the army.

198
00:15:56,654 --> 00:15:58,951
When I got discharged, you said, "Already?"

199
00:15:58,951 --> 00:16:00,878
That's not the same!

200
00:16:00,878 --> 00:16:03,435
Why are you yelling at me again?

201
00:16:03,435 --> 00:16:05,459
You silly girl!

202
00:16:05,459 --> 00:16:08,292
When your mom gives you something,
just take it!

203
00:16:08,292 --> 00:16:12,068
It breaks my heart
that I never did enough for you.

204
00:16:12,068 --> 00:16:13,840
Okay.

205
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,993
I'll take them.

206
00:16:19,413 --> 00:16:21,110
What do you want to eat?

207
00:16:21,110 --> 00:16:23,275
Let's just have dinner.

208
00:16:23,275 --> 00:16:25,020
Kimchi fried rice.

209
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,609
Fine.

210
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:30,114
Ju Young Jae! Come cut the kimchi!

211
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:32,860
I've been chopping things all day.

212
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,582
Move. Now.

213
00:16:40,352 --> 00:16:42,058
Chop it nice.

214
00:16:42,058 --> 00:16:43,841
Yes, ma'am.

215
00:16:56,473 --> 00:17:01,366
I never dreamed that
to hold one man in my arms,

216
00:17:01,366 --> 00:17:06,994
<i>I'd risk my life, take up a gun,
and cross a border.</i>

217
00:17:08,685 --> 00:17:11,555
<i>What an extraordinary man you are.</i>

218
00:17:13,635 --> 00:17:15,452
<i>So fearless.</i>

219
00:17:15,452 --> 00:17:18,928
<i>What an extraordinary woman you are.</i>

220
00:17:18,928 --> 00:17:21,194
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

221
00:17:21,194 --> 00:17:23,193
<i>Hold me.</i>

222
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:04,849
[Directed and Written by
Woo Soo Bin, Ju Yi Jae]

223
00:18:26,858 --> 00:18:29,009
- Good work.
- Thanks.

224
00:18:29,009 --> 00:18:30,379
It's a fine film.

225
00:18:30,379 --> 00:18:32,147
Thank you.

226
00:18:32,147 --> 00:18:36,581
At this rate, a release this year
should be no problem.

227
00:18:36,581 --> 00:18:37,595
Yeah.

228
00:18:37,595 --> 00:18:39,620
Good work, Director Woo.

229
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:41,928
Thank you for your hard work.

230
00:18:41,928 --> 00:18:44,893
- Thank you.
- Then let's continue this somewhere else.

231
00:18:44,893 --> 00:18:47,336
Yes. Please join us for dinner.

232
00:18:47,336 --> 00:18:49,138
I have a place reserved.

233
00:18:49,138 --> 00:18:50,598
Shall we?

234
00:18:50,598 --> 00:18:52,191
Let's go.

235
00:19:12,337 --> 00:19:13,789
Ian.

236
00:19:15,973 --> 00:19:18,973
I shouldn't say this as your CEO.

237
00:19:18,973 --> 00:19:23,053
But as your brother,
I always choose to go instead of stop.

238
00:19:23,053 --> 00:19:26,314
It's not too late. Go see Yi Jae.

239
00:19:27,659 --> 00:19:29,911
I said go.

240
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,841
Yeah.

241
00:19:34,566 --> 00:19:36,244
Ian!

242
00:19:36,244 --> 00:19:37,407
How are you getting there?

243
00:19:37,407 --> 00:19:39,680
Are you running all the way to the airport?

244
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:42,473
Here. Take the keys!

245
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:55,134
[Applicant Recommendation Letter]

246
00:19:55,134 --> 00:19:58,693
<i>I love the world Director Ju Yi Jae creates.</i>

247
00:19:59,534 --> 00:20:03,959
<i>Even in a world overrun with zombies,
she finds warmth.</i>

248
00:20:03,959 --> 00:20:06,608
<i>Even in an age filled with despair,</i>

249
00:20:06,608 --> 00:20:10,504
<i>she still finds hope.</i>

250
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:28,274
<i>She has a vision that is entirely her own.</i>

251
00:20:28,963 --> 00:20:33,160
<i>And it was a true honor</i>

252
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,975
<i>to be part of Director Ju Yi Jae's world.</i>

253
00:20:37,451 --> 00:20:39,359
[Incheon International Airport]

254
00:20:41,827 --> 00:20:46,145
<i>I still want to remain in that world.</i>

255
00:20:47,815 --> 00:20:50,483
<i>And it's still hard to let her go.</i>

256
00:20:54,543 --> 00:20:56,200
- Thank you.
<i>- But I know</i>

257
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:59,179
<i>she will do great things
in a much bigger world.</i>

258
00:20:59,179 --> 00:21:03,466
<i>So I give her my full support
on the road ahead.</i>

259
00:22:43,447 --> 00:22:46,258
<i>Without a doubt,</i>

260
00:22:47,228 --> 00:22:51,152
<i>Director Ju Yi Jae was
the best partner I have ever had.</i>

261
00:23:20,649 --> 00:23:24,613
[I can do this!]
[Greatness is seeing it through!]

262
00:24:15,470 --> 00:24:17,428
Come on, come on!

263
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:43,442
[Thursday, December 3, 2026
Final Draft Complete]

264
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:52,169
[Gyeongseong Love Song Screening, 8 PM]

265
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:02,990
[Gyeongseong Love Song VIP Screening]

266
00:25:02,990 --> 00:25:06,457
Thank you so much for coming
to the VIP screening.

267
00:25:06,457 --> 00:25:10,225
Now, please welcome
our directors and cast to the stage.

268
00:25:10,225 --> 00:25:13,597
A big round of applause, please.

269
00:25:13,597 --> 00:25:16,999
Looking good, Woo Soo Bin!

270
00:25:16,999 --> 00:25:19,437
You're amazing!

271
00:25:24,858 --> 00:25:26,026
Hello.

272
00:25:26,026 --> 00:25:29,213
I'm Woo Soo Bin,
director of "Gyeongseong Love Song."

273
00:25:29,213 --> 00:25:33,948
Our co-director, Ju Yi Jae,
unfortunately couldn't be with us today.

274
00:25:33,948 --> 00:25:36,572
Thank you for your understanding.

275
00:25:36,572 --> 00:25:40,998
Since you all took the time to be here,
I hope you laugh and cry all you want.

276
00:25:40,998 --> 00:25:42,035
And now...

277
00:25:42,035 --> 00:25:44,339
From action to romance,

278
00:25:44,339 --> 00:25:48,993
please welcome actress Oh Ha Na,
who shines in every genre.

279
00:25:48,993 --> 00:25:51,435
You're gorgeous, Oh Ha Na!

280
00:25:52,193 --> 00:25:57,181
Hello. I'm Oh Ha Na,
aiming to become the queen of romance

281
00:25:57,181 --> 00:25:59,309
with my big-screen debut.

282
00:26:00,601 --> 00:26:01,755
Hello.

283
00:26:01,755 --> 00:26:07,262
I'm rookie actor Sim Yu Geon,
playing Moo Gyeom.

284
00:26:07,262 --> 00:26:10,003
I hope you enjoy my performance. Thank you.

285
00:26:12,231 --> 00:26:15,993
We'll say one final goodbye before we go.

286
00:26:15,993 --> 00:26:18,160
One, two, three.

287
00:26:22,683 --> 00:26:26,881
Amazing. I wonder who they take after.

288
00:26:26,881 --> 00:26:29,437
Maybe I got lucky with my kids.

289
00:26:29,437 --> 00:26:31,753
Which one do you mean?

290
00:26:31,753 --> 00:26:34,730
- Oh my...
- Both, of course!

291
00:26:34,730 --> 00:26:36,805
Who invited you?

292
00:26:36,805 --> 00:26:39,188
- It's a good day, so I came.
- Don't touch me!

293
00:26:39,188 --> 00:26:40,885
- Get away.
- Just a second.

294
00:26:40,885 --> 00:26:42,180
Ma'am.

295
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:46,452
Your son and daughter turned out great,
just like you.

296
00:26:46,452 --> 00:26:47,924
You...

297
00:26:47,924 --> 00:26:50,321
Oh, did you change salons?

298
00:26:50,321 --> 00:26:51,403
Seriously...

299
00:26:51,403 --> 00:26:53,363
I'll let it slide today.

300
00:26:53,363 --> 00:26:56,566
If Director Ju were here today,

301
00:26:56,566 --> 00:26:59,625
she would've owned this stage.

302
00:26:59,625 --> 00:27:00,800
It's too bad.

303
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:02,067
True.

304
00:27:02,067 --> 00:27:05,121
Director Ju had one amazing voice.

305
00:27:05,121 --> 00:27:06,333
Gosh...

306
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:11,730
Feels like yesterday
she marched us all into CEO An's company.

307
00:27:11,730 --> 00:27:14,078
That was already a year ago.

308
00:27:15,054 --> 00:27:17,189
I wonder if she's doing okay.

309
00:27:19,478 --> 00:27:21,240
It's starting.

310
00:27:26,037 --> 00:27:27,607
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

311
00:27:27,607 --> 00:27:30,057
<i>The screening went well.</i>

312
00:27:30,777 --> 00:27:33,542
<i>The after-party was chaos.</i>

313
00:27:34,238 --> 00:27:38,240
<i>The Assistant Director went hard again tonight.</i>

314
00:27:41,256 --> 00:27:45,871
There's still one thing I regret.

315
00:27:45,871 --> 00:27:50,919
I never should've treated Director Ju that way.

316
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:55,634
You've told me that over ten times.

317
00:27:56,788 --> 00:27:59,128
Did I?

318
00:28:01,008 --> 00:28:02,849
Anyway...

319
00:28:02,849 --> 00:28:05,334
She may be younger than me,

320
00:28:05,334 --> 00:28:08,952
I think she's amazing.

321
00:28:08,952 --> 00:28:11,358
She already made her directorial debut,

322
00:28:11,358 --> 00:28:14,862
but still went abroad to learn more.

323
00:28:14,862 --> 00:28:17,652
That takes real courage.

324
00:28:17,652 --> 00:28:21,741
I could never do that. Never.

325
00:28:21,741 --> 00:28:23,074
You said that too.

326
00:28:23,074 --> 00:28:24,892
Right.

327
00:28:24,892 --> 00:28:26,757
I did.

328
00:28:26,757 --> 00:28:28,642
Then...

329
00:28:28,642 --> 00:28:32,265
Should we save the rest for round three?

330
00:28:32,265 --> 00:28:35,799
Round one was official.
Round two was out of courtesy.

331
00:28:35,799 --> 00:28:38,213
I've done my duty for the night.

332
00:28:38,213 --> 00:28:40,846
Come on!

333
00:28:40,846 --> 00:28:43,388
Round three is for romance.

334
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:45,500
Round four is for loyalty.

335
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:47,449
No.

336
00:28:48,472 --> 00:28:50,822
Let's call it a night.

337
00:28:50,822 --> 00:28:54,780
I miss loyal Director Ju.

338
00:28:54,780 --> 00:28:58,852
What time is it in Canada now?

339
00:29:00,818 --> 00:29:02,556
Director Ju.

340
00:29:02,556 --> 00:29:05,238
Director Ju...

341
00:29:07,623 --> 00:29:09,960
[Director Ju]

342
00:29:20,751 --> 00:29:22,443
<i>Hello?</i>

343
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:26,248
<i>Hello?</i>

344
00:29:26,248 --> 00:29:28,157
<i>Assistant Director?</i>

345
00:29:31,328 --> 00:29:34,097
<i>Are you calling about today's screening?</i>

346
00:29:34,097 --> 00:29:35,987
<i>How did it go?</i>

347
00:29:38,931 --> 00:29:40,391
<i>Huh?</i>

348
00:29:44,762 --> 00:29:47,042
<i>Are you there?</i>

349
00:29:48,859 --> 00:29:51,174
<i>What is this...</i>

350
00:29:52,168 --> 00:29:55,428
<i>This call is expensive. I'm hanging up!</i>

351
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:02,471
<i>Do you know?</i>

352
00:30:04,427 --> 00:30:07,196
<i>For 24 seconds,</i>

353
00:30:08,098 --> 00:30:10,312
<i>we were together.</i>

354
00:30:42,804 --> 00:30:44,496
What are you listening to?

355
00:30:47,336 --> 00:30:49,947
My dad playing the guitar.

356
00:30:49,947 --> 00:30:51,733
Oh, really?

357
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:07,644
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

358
00:31:15,711 --> 00:31:17,535
You can lean on me.

359
00:31:34,478 --> 00:31:36,233
<i>Yu Geon.</i>

360
00:31:37,301 --> 00:31:40,354
<i>When should we open our canned pineapple?</i>

361
00:31:42,009 --> 00:31:43,742
<i>In ten thousand years?</i>

362
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:53,218
<i>Our two leads get their perfect happy ending.</i>

363
00:31:55,122 --> 00:31:57,918
[On-screen lovers become real...
Oh Ha Na and Sim Yu Geon spotted dating]

364
00:31:59,090 --> 00:32:02,344
<i>Maybe. Maybe not.</i>

365
00:32:02,344 --> 00:32:04,026
No way.

366
00:32:04,901 --> 00:32:07,200
Sim Yu Geon!

367
00:32:21,523 --> 00:32:23,039
[Search All: Choi Sa Rang]

368
00:32:24,230 --> 00:32:25,250
Choi Sa Rang?

369
00:32:25,250 --> 00:32:27,370
[Choi Sa Rang]

370
00:32:27,370 --> 00:32:29,968
[Essay: Easy Love, Hard Love]

371
00:32:34,766 --> 00:32:35,800
[Choi Sa Rang]

372
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:37,909
[Book Search]

373
00:32:38,874 --> 00:32:40,544
Done.

374
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:46,345
[Choi Sa Rang]

375
00:32:47,141 --> 00:32:48,480
Done.

376
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:50,396
Now that's how you market.

377
00:32:50,396 --> 00:32:52,513
I'm a genius.

378
00:32:52,513 --> 00:32:54,250
[Trending New Books]

379
00:32:59,525 --> 00:33:01,246
Where did they all go?

380
00:33:01,246 --> 00:33:03,265
What...

381
00:33:03,265 --> 00:33:04,676
Wait.

382
00:33:04,676 --> 00:33:08,614
Excuse me. All my books are gone.

383
00:33:08,614 --> 00:33:11,367
"Easy Love, Hard Love."

384
00:33:11,367 --> 00:33:14,514
That gentleman over there...

385
00:33:21,001 --> 00:33:22,863
In Uk?

386
00:33:27,882 --> 00:33:29,495
Oh, no.

387
00:33:29,495 --> 00:33:31,381
You caught me.

388
00:33:41,907 --> 00:33:47,419
<i>As for the people we know,
their ending seems to be open.</i>

389
00:33:49,305 --> 00:33:53,329
This is something I'm personally curious about.

390
00:33:53,329 --> 00:33:59,091
In this film, you're credited
under your real name, Woo Soo Bin.

391
00:33:59,091 --> 00:34:01,758
Is there a special reason?

392
00:34:01,758 --> 00:34:06,408
Since I came back to Korea,
I wanted to be called by my own name.

393
00:34:07,054 --> 00:34:12,142
Every step I've taken was
toward getting that name back.

394
00:34:13,234 --> 00:34:15,098
And finally...

395
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:18,173
I'm here.

396
00:34:24,274 --> 00:34:26,118
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

397
00:34:26,118 --> 00:34:30,515
<i>I hope this isn't where my story ends.</i>

398
00:35:18,539 --> 00:35:20,565
<i>I miss you.</i>

399
00:35:20,565 --> 00:35:22,219
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

400
00:35:31,187 --> 00:35:33,140
<i>I guess...</i>

401
00:35:35,544 --> 00:35:37,988
<i>I still haven't gotten over you.</i>

402
00:35:41,437 --> 00:35:46,336
<i>I guess I still don't want to wake up
from this dream.</i>

403
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:08,252
[One year later]

404
00:36:08,252 --> 00:36:10,268
Woo Soo Bin!

405
00:36:14,465 --> 00:36:16,396
Woo Soo Bin!

406
00:36:17,858 --> 00:36:22,315
What happened to this place?
It's a total pigsty.

407
00:36:22,315 --> 00:36:25,134
Why do you always leave your socks unmatched?

408
00:36:25,134 --> 00:36:27,795
What are you even doing?

409
00:36:27,795 --> 00:36:30,315
The festival crew is coming.

410
00:36:30,315 --> 00:36:31,913
I said I'm not doing it.

411
00:36:31,913 --> 00:36:34,736
Just give them a quick greeting.

412
00:36:34,736 --> 00:36:36,613
No.

413
00:36:36,613 --> 00:36:40,165
- What?
- I said no.

414
00:36:40,165 --> 00:36:42,370
You don't want to?

415
00:36:42,370 --> 00:36:44,534
Then write a script.

416
00:36:44,534 --> 00:36:46,053
Nice try.

417
00:36:46,053 --> 00:36:47,610
Stop nagging me.

418
00:36:47,610 --> 00:36:49,530
I'm not joking.

419
00:36:49,530 --> 00:36:52,588
How long will you keep moping around?

420
00:36:52,588 --> 00:36:54,770
You need to work so I can make money too.

421
00:36:54,770 --> 00:36:58,104
You keep turning down every script.

422
00:36:58,104 --> 00:36:59,921
Come on.

423
00:36:59,921 --> 00:37:01,972
You have Director Park and Director Kim.

424
00:37:01,972 --> 00:37:03,861
Tell them to work hard.

425
00:37:03,861 --> 00:37:07,519
They're working hard looking for scripts.

426
00:37:07,519 --> 00:37:11,021
But you already have one.

427
00:37:11,021 --> 00:37:12,805
What script do I have?

428
00:37:12,805 --> 00:37:15,194
"Dream." The one you wrote in the States.

429
00:37:15,194 --> 00:37:18,042
- Oh...
- You remember?

430
00:37:18,042 --> 00:37:20,574
Let's make it. I like that story.

431
00:37:20,574 --> 00:37:23,065
- I don't have it.
- What?

432
00:37:23,065 --> 00:37:25,403
- Yi Jae has it.
- What?

433
00:37:25,403 --> 00:37:27,362
Did you at least scan it?

434
00:37:35,255 --> 00:37:36,548
Let's break up.

435
00:37:36,548 --> 00:37:37,883
We really should.

436
00:37:37,883 --> 00:37:42,133
I'm so sick of this.
Let's say goodbye for real.

437
00:37:42,133 --> 00:37:45,118
I'm already saying goodbye every day.

438
00:37:48,543 --> 00:37:49,708
Hey.

439
00:37:49,708 --> 00:37:53,868
Yi Jae would hate seeing you like this.

440
00:37:54,557 --> 00:37:56,367
This year's Geumseong Film Festival...

441
00:37:56,367 --> 00:37:58,657
Sim Yu Geon and Oh Ha Na are hosting.

442
00:37:58,657 --> 00:38:02,357
They both won Best Newcomer last year,

443
00:38:02,357 --> 00:38:06,453
so there's a special screening
of "Gyeongseong Love Song."

444
00:38:06,453 --> 00:38:07,637
Soo Bin.

445
00:38:07,637 --> 00:38:11,422
I know what "Gyeongseong Love Song"
means to you.

446
00:38:11,422 --> 00:38:16,463
Use this chance to say a proper final goodbye,

447
00:38:16,463 --> 00:38:18,595
and let it go now.

448
00:38:21,793 --> 00:38:23,272
In Uk.

449
00:38:24,633 --> 00:38:27,920
Even you can't stand looking at me?

450
00:38:28,559 --> 00:38:30,299
Am I that pathetic?

451
00:38:33,419 --> 00:38:34,905
Yeah.

452
00:38:35,911 --> 00:38:38,643
I think I'm pathetic too.

453
00:38:38,643 --> 00:38:42,449
Yi Jae will shine even without me.

454
00:38:43,150 --> 00:38:45,313
I'm hopeless.

455
00:38:48,518 --> 00:38:50,144
I'll do it.

456
00:38:54,895 --> 00:38:56,665
Director Woo!

457
00:38:56,665 --> 00:38:58,696
- It's been so long.
- Hello.

458
00:38:58,696 --> 00:39:00,426
- How have you been?
- Please come in.

459
00:39:00,426 --> 00:39:01,912
They're here.

460
00:39:01,912 --> 00:39:04,397
- Hello.
- You made it.

461
00:39:08,086 --> 00:39:09,710
Director Woo?

462
00:39:09,710 --> 00:39:12,731
- It's been so long.
- Right.

463
00:39:12,731 --> 00:39:14,158
You've met before, right?

464
00:39:14,158 --> 00:39:16,563
- He's in charge of today's festival shoot.
- I see.

465
00:39:16,563 --> 00:39:18,689
Director Woo, don't you remember me?

466
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:22,083
Does it look like I forgot?

467
00:39:23,316 --> 00:39:26,113
You've gotten even pricklier.

468
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:27,613
Anyway...

469
00:39:28,223 --> 00:39:32,020
I left the network
and started a small production company.

470
00:39:32,719 --> 00:39:34,415
So...

471
00:39:34,415 --> 00:39:37,309
Looking forward to working with you today.

472
00:39:37,309 --> 00:39:39,249
Let's see.

473
00:39:39,249 --> 00:39:41,337
Where should we film?

474
00:39:41,337 --> 00:39:43,942
The view is incredible.

475
00:39:43,942 --> 00:39:46,470
The balcony might be too cold.

476
00:39:46,470 --> 00:39:48,138
This spot looks good.

477
00:39:48,138 --> 00:39:50,944
Yes, let's shoot here.

478
00:39:51,642 --> 00:39:53,265
Would you like some coffee?

479
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:57,052
Yes, please! Iced Americano, decaf.

480
00:40:03,543 --> 00:40:04,807
Do you have a script?

481
00:40:04,807 --> 00:40:05,847
No.

482
00:40:05,847 --> 00:40:07,957
This plays before the screening, right?

483
00:40:07,957 --> 00:40:09,180
How long do you need?

484
00:40:09,180 --> 00:40:10,184
Well...

485
00:40:10,184 --> 00:40:12,214
About a minute is fine.

486
00:40:12,214 --> 00:40:13,788
Oh, right.

487
00:40:14,454 --> 00:40:18,011
Where's Ju Yi Jae? I don't see her.

488
00:40:18,011 --> 00:40:19,867
Jeez.

489
00:40:20,491 --> 00:40:22,248
Did you two split up?

490
00:40:22,248 --> 00:40:24,800
She is pretty intense to work with. Right?

491
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:28,324
She is filming in Canada.

492
00:40:28,324 --> 00:40:29,986
Canada?

493
00:40:30,681 --> 00:40:34,784
She owes me big time.

494
00:40:34,784 --> 00:40:37,252
- Sorry?
- Just a moment...

495
00:40:38,522 --> 00:40:39,847
But Director Woo,

496
00:40:39,847 --> 00:40:43,067
your style has gotten a lot more relaxed.

497
00:40:43,067 --> 00:40:45,352
Now you finally look like a director.

498
00:40:45,352 --> 00:40:46,980
Are you shooting anything these days?

499
00:40:46,980 --> 00:40:48,662
- Sir.
- Yes?

500
00:40:48,662 --> 00:40:51,736
Are we filming or not?

501
00:40:51,736 --> 00:40:53,293
Let's get started.

502
00:40:53,293 --> 00:40:54,970
I was just about to.

503
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:57,737
Could you just take off that hoodie?

504
00:40:57,737 --> 00:40:58,927
I'll take it off.

505
00:40:58,927 --> 00:41:01,334
Yes, please.

506
00:41:09,762 --> 00:41:12,047
Oh my gosh... It's been ages.

507
00:41:12,047 --> 00:41:14,799
How have you been?

508
00:41:14,799 --> 00:41:16,227
I missed you so much.

509
00:41:16,227 --> 00:41:18,973
Wow. You look so pretty.

510
00:42:02,021 --> 00:42:03,954
Hey.

511
00:42:03,954 --> 00:42:05,886
I thought you were in Canada.

512
00:42:05,886 --> 00:42:07,411
You look great.

513
00:42:07,411 --> 00:42:08,695
What are you doing here?

514
00:42:08,695 --> 00:42:10,997
I'm just here for...

515
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:22,105
Hey.

516
00:42:22,690 --> 00:42:24,591
I can't breathe.

517
00:42:27,297 --> 00:42:30,015
Oh, right. I was making coffee.

518
00:42:30,015 --> 00:42:32,758
- Right! The coffee!
- Camera! Camera!

519
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:34,961
I really want to film this.

520
00:42:34,961 --> 00:42:36,186
Come get your coffee.

521
00:42:36,186 --> 00:42:38,181
I made it cold enough to freeze you solid.

522
00:42:38,181 --> 00:42:39,552
Decaf, right?

523
00:42:39,552 --> 00:42:40,978
Where are you?

524
00:42:40,978 --> 00:42:42,931
That bistro again?

525
00:42:42,931 --> 00:42:45,619
You're reading?

526
00:42:49,684 --> 00:42:51,443
You're real.

527
00:42:52,609 --> 00:42:54,731
You're really Ju Yi Jae.

528
00:42:54,731 --> 00:42:56,626
Have you been well?

529
00:43:05,737 --> 00:43:06,941
What is this?

530
00:43:06,941 --> 00:43:09,545
Curtains shut in the middle of the day?

531
00:43:10,308 --> 00:43:11,967
What a mess.

532
00:43:11,967 --> 00:43:14,402
You used to be so neat.

533
00:43:15,154 --> 00:43:16,971
When did you get here?

534
00:43:16,971 --> 00:43:18,767
Early this morning.

535
00:43:20,354 --> 00:43:21,898
Why?

536
00:43:21,898 --> 00:43:24,000
Guess why.

537
00:43:25,214 --> 00:43:27,845
The Geumseong Film Festival opens in two weeks.

538
00:43:27,845 --> 00:43:31,075
I'm nominated for the Rising Director Award.

539
00:43:31,736 --> 00:43:33,227
I see.

540
00:43:34,496 --> 00:43:37,251
What? No congratulations?

541
00:43:37,251 --> 00:43:40,452
After the festival... are you going back?

542
00:43:40,452 --> 00:43:41,857
I don't know.

543
00:43:41,857 --> 00:43:43,813
That depends on you.

544
00:43:46,668 --> 00:43:50,539
Then what do I have to do?

545
00:43:50,539 --> 00:43:52,532
Do you have a girlfriend?

546
00:43:54,612 --> 00:43:56,472
Guess not.

547
00:43:57,635 --> 00:44:00,338
- Want to make a movie with me?
- What?

548
00:44:05,852 --> 00:44:07,979
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

549
00:44:07,979 --> 00:44:12,243
I found out in Canada
that you wrote my recommendation.

550
00:44:12,904 --> 00:44:17,690
I think I've grown enough
to stand proudly beside you now.

551
00:44:17,690 --> 00:44:20,323
Make a movie with me, Woo Soo Bin.

552
00:44:22,144 --> 00:44:23,774
Can I kiss you?

553
00:44:23,774 --> 00:44:26,017
- Are you going to?
- Yes.

554
00:44:26,624 --> 00:44:27,995
No.

555
00:44:27,995 --> 00:44:30,294
I meant the movie.

556
00:44:35,660 --> 00:44:37,087
Yes.

557
00:44:43,893 --> 00:44:45,670
Directors?

558
00:44:46,313 --> 00:44:47,456
Excuse me.

559
00:44:47,456 --> 00:44:49,154
Why aren't you coming out?

560
00:44:49,154 --> 00:44:52,375
Can we clock out now?

561
00:44:54,466 --> 00:44:57,320
What are they doing?

562
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:59,533
Directors.

563
00:44:59,533 --> 00:45:01,596
Could you open the door?

564
00:45:07,749 --> 00:45:13,289
The Rising Director Award
at the 16th Geumseong Film Festival goes to...

565
00:45:15,534 --> 00:45:17,664
Director Ju Yi Jae of "Love Like A Dream."

566
00:45:17,664 --> 00:45:19,344
Congratulations.

567
00:45:19,344 --> 00:45:22,139
Director Ju Yi Jae completed
"Love Like A Dream"

568
00:45:22,139 --> 00:45:25,389
through the International
Cinema Residency Program.

569
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:28,023
The film was praised for
bringing to life a fantastical world

570
00:45:28,023 --> 00:45:32,670
between dreams and reality
with her own convincing vision.

571
00:45:38,617 --> 00:45:40,789
Congratulations, Yi Jae.

572
00:45:44,051 --> 00:45:46,437
I won an award!

573
00:45:50,417 --> 00:45:52,436
Thank you.

574
00:45:54,361 --> 00:45:58,505
"Love Like A Dream"
was a bold challenge for me.

575
00:45:58,505 --> 00:46:00,684
My first solo film.

576
00:46:00,684 --> 00:46:03,518
Writing a script in an unfamiliar place.

577
00:46:03,518 --> 00:46:06,731
Working with an international crew...

578
00:46:06,731 --> 00:46:09,574
It was so hard.

579
00:46:10,267 --> 00:46:13,524
But I held on for one reason.

580
00:46:14,191 --> 00:46:20,473
I wanted to become someone worthy
of standing beside the person I love.

581
00:46:21,862 --> 00:46:24,825
I loved my dream with all my heart.

582
00:46:24,825 --> 00:46:27,562
<i>Yes. Let's make it together.</i>

583
00:46:27,562 --> 00:46:28,862
<i>Come here!</i>

584
00:46:28,862 --> 00:46:30,667
<i>- Come here.
- Stop!</i>

585
00:46:30,667 --> 00:46:31,998
<i>Let me go!</i>

586
00:46:31,998 --> 00:46:35,462
The more I loved it, the more I hated it.

587
00:46:35,462 --> 00:46:37,420
<i>You bastard.</i>

588
00:46:39,675 --> 00:46:43,498
I tried to forget it,
but in the end, I came back.

589
00:46:43,498 --> 00:46:45,615
<i>Excuse me.</i>

590
00:46:52,715 --> 00:46:55,894
Right now, it feels like...

591
00:46:55,894 --> 00:47:00,873
I went through a love like war
and somehow reached a dramatic truce.

592
00:47:01,819 --> 00:47:07,262
Someday, we may go at each other
like enemies again.

593
00:47:07,262 --> 00:47:09,719
But I'm not worried.

594
00:47:09,719 --> 00:47:14,677
Because I've become a bigger person.

595
00:47:15,993 --> 00:47:21,675
So I'll keep fighting this love like war.

596
00:47:21,675 --> 00:47:23,568
Thank you!

597
00:48:28,574 --> 00:48:30,024
<i>Ready...</i>

598
00:48:30,024 --> 00:48:31,859
<i>Action!</i>

599
00:48:36,433 --> 00:48:38,990
<i>Enough with the filming.</i>

600
00:48:38,990 --> 00:48:41,146
<i>Come taste this.</i>

601
00:48:43,579 --> 00:48:45,435
<i>Good! It's just right.</i>

602
00:48:45,435 --> 00:48:47,780
<i>- Is it too bland?</i>
- No.

603
00:48:48,764 --> 00:48:50,304
Perfect.

604
00:48:52,598 --> 00:48:54,688
- Mom.
- Yes?

605
00:48:54,688 --> 00:48:58,108
Is there anything you want to do?

606
00:48:58,108 --> 00:48:59,538
Why all of a sudden?

607
00:48:59,538 --> 00:49:04,315
I heard Soo Bin's mom
and the guesthouse grandma travel together.

608
00:49:04,315 --> 00:49:07,120
Want to go on a weeklong trip with me?

609
00:49:07,120 --> 00:49:08,514
Forget it.

610
00:49:08,514 --> 00:49:11,211
I can't just leave my customers.

611
00:49:11,211 --> 00:49:13,971
Then let's close the shop.

612
00:49:13,971 --> 00:49:16,668
Young Jae makes money now too.

613
00:49:16,668 --> 00:49:18,342
Yi Jae.

614
00:49:20,561 --> 00:49:23,258
I was too busy scraping by.

615
00:49:23,258 --> 00:49:26,634
The shop never made me happy.

616
00:49:26,634 --> 00:49:30,224
Every morning, opening the shop felt so heavy.

617
00:49:30,841 --> 00:49:33,779
But these days, the door feels lighter.

618
00:49:35,128 --> 00:49:38,453
I guess I'm finally at ease

619
00:49:38,453 --> 00:49:41,342
now that you and Young Jae
have found your own way.

620
00:49:42,523 --> 00:49:46,316
For now, I want to run the shop in peace.

621
00:49:48,497 --> 00:49:52,455
<i>When I get tired of it, I'll quit. Okay?</i>

622
00:49:55,233 --> 00:49:58,483
Once you quit, you have to travel with me.

623
00:49:58,483 --> 00:50:00,234
Okay.

624
00:50:00,234 --> 00:50:01,867
Promise.

625
00:50:03,070 --> 00:50:05,064
<i>Like this?</i>

626
00:50:09,988 --> 00:50:12,426
Then I'm off.

627
00:50:12,426 --> 00:50:13,977
Where are you going?

628
00:50:13,977 --> 00:50:15,470
To see Soo Bin.

629
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:17,976
- Hey, Yi Jae.
- Yeah?

630
00:50:17,976 --> 00:50:20,882
All that talking, and you forgot to sign?

631
00:50:20,882 --> 00:50:23,114
Oh, right.

632
00:50:24,844 --> 00:50:26,544
Wait.

633
00:50:26,544 --> 00:50:29,123
- Here it is.
- Oh my.

634
00:50:32,988 --> 00:50:36,484
But do these people even know who I am?

635
00:50:36,484 --> 00:50:37,538
Of course.

636
00:50:37,538 --> 00:50:39,884
Film director Ju Yi Jae.

637
00:50:40,711 --> 00:50:43,623
I doubt they've all seen my movies.

638
00:50:43,623 --> 00:50:45,963
Yeah, they haven't.

639
00:50:45,963 --> 00:50:47,381
What?

640
00:50:47,381 --> 00:50:51,382
So I told them, "No movie, no autograph."

641
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:53,267
I knew it.

642
00:50:54,241 --> 00:50:56,532
- Alright...
- Get to it.

643
00:50:56,532 --> 00:50:59,309
"'Gyeongseong Love Song'

644
00:50:59,309 --> 00:51:00,862
Director.

645
00:51:00,862 --> 00:51:02,902
Ju Yi Jae."

646
00:51:02,902 --> 00:51:04,567
How's that?

647
00:51:04,567 --> 00:51:07,573
- Great!
- Right?

648
00:51:08,867 --> 00:51:11,337
Are your mom and Grandma coming today?

649
00:51:11,337 --> 00:51:14,083
They should be arriving right about now.

650
00:51:20,074 --> 00:51:22,111
Guys! We're here!

651
00:51:22,111 --> 00:51:23,464
Grandma!

652
00:51:23,464 --> 00:51:24,498
Soo Bin.

653
00:51:24,498 --> 00:51:26,488
Yi Jae, get in.

654
00:51:26,488 --> 00:51:27,932
Get in.

655
00:51:33,839 --> 00:51:36,292
Let's go!

656
00:51:36,292 --> 00:51:40,362
- I brought something.
- She worked hard to find it.

657
00:51:40,362 --> 00:51:42,102
[Sea Trip: Saw the ocean with Hwa Yeon today]
Wow.

658
00:51:42,102 --> 00:51:44,542
All the way to Gangneung?

659
00:51:45,185 --> 00:51:47,819
I thought all oceans were the same.

660
00:51:47,819 --> 00:51:50,905
But the one there was different from ours.

661
00:51:50,905 --> 00:51:55,268
The waves here are calm, like me.
Like they've lived a whole life.

662
00:51:55,268 --> 00:51:59,073
But Gangneung's waves were so blue and strong,

663
00:51:59,073 --> 00:52:01,121
just like you kids.

664
00:52:01,121 --> 00:52:04,791
To me, you looked just like
the waves in Gangneung.

665
00:52:04,791 --> 00:52:06,376
Yeah?

666
00:52:06,376 --> 00:52:11,503
She kept grumbling until we left,
saying, "Why go anywhere at my age?"

667
00:52:11,503 --> 00:52:13,592
But once we got there...

668
00:52:14,337 --> 00:52:17,471
She had more energy than I did.

669
00:52:17,471 --> 00:52:19,900
I can't travel with Hwa Yeon anymore.

670
00:52:19,900 --> 00:52:22,553
We walk 30 minutes, and she says, "Let's rest."

671
00:52:22,553 --> 00:52:24,643
Then, "Let's get coffee."

672
00:52:24,643 --> 00:52:26,667
We barely looked around.

673
00:52:26,667 --> 00:52:30,609
We didn't go there
just to sit and drink coffee.

674
00:52:30,609 --> 00:52:32,069
Am I wrong?

675
00:52:32,069 --> 00:52:35,081
You're right. Grandma is right.

676
00:52:35,081 --> 00:52:39,408
Then where do you want to go next, Grandma?

677
00:52:39,408 --> 00:52:43,038
<i>I could even go to the States now.</i>

678
00:52:43,038 --> 00:52:46,584
<i>I want to fly on a plane before I die.</i>

679
00:52:46,584 --> 00:52:48,322
Let's go together.

680
00:52:48,322 --> 00:52:51,786
No! Not with you!

681
00:52:51,786 --> 00:52:54,183
Come on. You'd miss me.

682
00:52:54,183 --> 00:52:55,551
Miss you? Please.

683
00:52:55,551 --> 00:52:58,759
- Come with me.
- Then just go with me.

684
00:52:58,759 --> 00:53:01,301
- Should I?
- Yi Jae, you come too.

685
00:53:01,301 --> 00:53:04,393
So the main character finally escapes!

686
00:53:04,393 --> 00:53:05,809
But then, the twist!

687
00:53:05,809 --> 00:53:08,765
Right in front of him,
the ending credits start rolling!

688
00:53:08,765 --> 00:53:09,937
With the game company logo.

689
00:53:09,937 --> 00:53:11,641
Chills!

690
00:53:11,641 --> 00:53:13,318
He was inside the game all along.

691
00:53:13,318 --> 00:53:14,350
What do you think?

692
00:53:14,350 --> 00:53:16,874
Can you feel it? Yeah?

693
00:53:18,070 --> 00:53:20,527
If this becomes a movie, it'll be huge.

694
00:53:20,527 --> 00:53:22,911
- The braised radish is good today, right?
- Try this too.

695
00:53:22,911 --> 00:53:25,664
Come on, listen! This is my dream!

696
00:53:25,664 --> 00:53:27,374
My novel becoming a movie!

697
00:53:27,374 --> 00:53:29,420
Kim Jin Su.

698
00:53:30,970 --> 00:53:32,993
Yi Jae!

699
00:53:35,361 --> 00:53:36,383
You useless man.

700
00:53:36,383 --> 00:53:39,804
- Seong Chan.
- I told you to pick up Seong Chan today.

701
00:53:39,804 --> 00:53:41,681
- Oh, right...
- "Oh, right?"

702
00:53:41,681 --> 00:53:43,651
"Dream," my foot.

703
00:53:43,651 --> 00:53:46,691
My dream is for you to become human.

704
00:53:46,691 --> 00:53:47,728
Get over here.

705
00:53:47,728 --> 00:53:49,528
I'll make you human.

706
00:53:49,528 --> 00:53:51,937
- Okay! Stay back!
- Come here!

707
00:53:52,975 --> 00:53:54,092
What is that?

708
00:53:54,092 --> 00:53:56,699
This? A camera.

709
00:53:56,699 --> 00:53:58,212
Want to see?

710
00:53:58,899 --> 00:54:02,166
That seems a little violent for a kid to watch.

711
00:54:02,166 --> 00:54:03,363
It's okay.

712
00:54:03,363 --> 00:54:06,201
I'm in elementary school now.

713
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:07,263
Seong Chan.

714
00:54:07,263 --> 00:54:09,287
What do you want to be when you grow up?

715
00:54:09,287 --> 00:54:13,318
Mom said I should become anything but Dad.

716
00:54:14,488 --> 00:54:16,241
Their spicy fish stew is amazing.

717
00:54:16,241 --> 00:54:18,675
Let's come back. This place is my new favorite.

718
00:54:18,675 --> 00:54:20,377
I'm full.

719
00:54:21,251 --> 00:54:24,231
[SimSim Fisheries]
Looks like he's doing well.

720
00:54:25,873 --> 00:54:26,977
<i>Hey.</i>

721
00:54:26,977 --> 00:54:29,144
<i>You stay seated.</i>

722
00:54:29,144 --> 00:54:31,208
I'm proud of him.

723
00:54:31,208 --> 00:54:33,727
Why are you proud of my brother?

724
00:54:33,727 --> 00:54:36,005
He's my brother-in-law.

725
00:54:36,005 --> 00:54:37,097
What?

726
00:54:37,734 --> 00:54:39,450
I should help him out.

727
00:54:39,450 --> 00:54:40,917
Brother-in-law, wait.

728
00:54:40,917 --> 00:54:42,321
Please stay seated.

729
00:54:42,321 --> 00:54:44,574
- No, I'll help.
- No, it's okay.

730
00:54:44,574 --> 00:54:46,138
Please...

731
00:54:46,138 --> 00:54:47,491
My brother-in-law.

732
00:54:47,491 --> 00:54:49,435
Gosh... "Brother-in-law?"

733
00:54:49,435 --> 00:54:51,928
Unbelievable.

734
00:54:55,921 --> 00:54:57,301
<i>Brother-in-law.</i>

735
00:54:58,218 --> 00:54:59,948
<i>I love you.</i>

736
00:54:59,948 --> 00:55:01,241
<i>Love you too.</i>

737
00:55:04,108 --> 00:55:06,644
I'm curious about something.

738
00:55:06,644 --> 00:55:07,934
What?

739
00:55:07,934 --> 00:55:09,847
Didn't you miss me?

740
00:55:09,847 --> 00:55:11,584
What kind of question is that?

741
00:55:11,584 --> 00:55:13,632
Then how could you not call me once?

742
00:55:13,632 --> 00:55:15,037
You're so cold.

743
00:55:15,037 --> 00:55:16,378
I did.

744
00:55:16,378 --> 00:55:17,816
Sorry?

745
00:55:17,816 --> 00:55:18,819
Nothing.

746
00:55:18,819 --> 00:55:23,232
Then did you lose sleep,
skip meals, drink, and cry?

747
00:55:23,232 --> 00:55:25,158
Who do you think I am?

748
00:55:25,158 --> 00:55:28,067
It wasn't that bad.

749
00:55:30,361 --> 00:55:32,412
<i>"Ju Yi Jae..."</i>

750
00:55:32,412 --> 00:55:35,758
<i>Damn it. Here he goes again.</i>

751
00:55:35,758 --> 00:55:37,960
<i>Don't disappear!</i>

752
00:55:37,960 --> 00:55:39,022
<i>No!</i>

753
00:55:39,022 --> 00:55:41,782
<i>Telepathy. Telepathy.</i>

754
00:55:41,782 --> 00:55:43,732
<i>Ju Yi Jae.</i>

755
00:55:43,732 --> 00:55:47,095
<i>Come here right now.</i>

756
00:55:47,095 --> 00:55:49,119
<i>Right now.</i>

757
00:55:49,119 --> 00:55:51,772
<i>Mom, that man is weird.</i>

758
00:55:51,772 --> 00:55:53,349
<i>Don't stare.</i>

759
00:55:53,349 --> 00:55:54,923
<i>Come here right now!</i>

760
00:55:54,923 --> 00:55:56,794
<i>Oh my gosh...</i>

761
00:55:56,794 --> 00:55:59,318
<i>I used to make hangover soup for my daughter.</i>

762
00:55:59,318 --> 00:56:02,336
<i>Now I have to make yours too?</i>

763
00:56:02,336 --> 00:56:03,322
<i>Hello.</i>

764
00:56:03,322 --> 00:56:06,045
<i>Yi Jae, don't go...</i>

765
00:56:17,921 --> 00:56:19,614
I was...

766
00:56:20,681 --> 00:56:22,760
perfectly calm while I waited.

767
00:56:22,760 --> 00:56:24,963
But you did wait.

768
00:56:26,063 --> 00:56:28,843
Of course.

769
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:30,620
You were coming back.

770
00:56:30,620 --> 00:56:32,460
I could've settled down in Canada.

771
00:56:32,460 --> 00:56:34,600
I'd report you for overstaying.

772
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:36,772
I could've stayed there legally.

773
00:56:36,772 --> 00:56:39,110
Then I would've gone there.

774
00:56:39,110 --> 00:56:41,837
I might not have welcomed you.

775
00:56:41,837 --> 00:56:44,601
Why wouldn't you?

776
00:56:44,601 --> 00:56:47,357
Maybe I got a new boyfriend.

777
00:56:47,357 --> 00:56:49,250
A handsome boyfriend.

778
00:56:49,250 --> 00:56:51,733
A sexy boyfriend.

779
00:56:52,783 --> 00:56:54,386
More than me?

780
00:56:57,834 --> 00:56:58,978
Get home safe.

781
00:56:58,978 --> 00:57:01,291
Sexy, handsome Soo Bin.

782
00:57:04,831 --> 00:57:06,440
Yi Jae.

783
00:57:11,235 --> 00:57:12,795
Will you...

784
00:57:13,559 --> 00:57:15,643
stay with me tonight?

785
00:57:41,317 --> 00:57:42,928
Hurry!

786
00:58:22,615 --> 00:58:24,220
That tickles.

787
00:58:24,220 --> 00:58:25,933
Deal with it.

788
00:58:33,161 --> 00:58:35,864
I lost this.

789
00:58:35,864 --> 00:58:39,074
Tie your hair, then keep going.

790
00:58:39,074 --> 00:58:40,551
Wait.

791
00:58:40,551 --> 00:58:42,780
Were you at the airport that day?

792
00:58:47,716 --> 00:58:49,062
Yes.

793
00:58:49,924 --> 00:58:51,760
And...

794
00:58:53,377 --> 00:58:55,012
this.

795
00:59:04,989 --> 00:59:06,666
What is this?

796
00:59:11,659 --> 00:59:13,468
My dream.

797
00:59:16,711 --> 00:59:18,043
Cut!

798
00:59:18,638 --> 00:59:19,933
"Cut?"

799
00:59:39,988 --> 00:59:41,344
Okay!

800
00:59:41,344 --> 00:59:42,902
Okay!

801
00:59:54,629 --> 00:59:57,994
[Dream to You]

802
01:00:08,816 --> 01:00:11,642
[Thank you for watching "Dream to You"]
